==Restrictions==
Max # of Deployable Cats: 15

==Battleground==
*9 [[Sinner Snache]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*2 [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 53.33~56.67 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,700f</sup>.
*1 [[Maawth]] spawns after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>.
*1 [[Condemned Peng]] spawns after 43.33 seconds<sup>1,300f</sup>.
*2 [[Maawth]]s spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 110~113.33 seconds<sup>3,300f~3,400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Infernal Pegasus Deonil]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Cumulus Gallus]] spawns.
**Infinite [[Sinner Snache]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
**4 [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 43.33~46.67 seconds<sup>1,300f~1,400f</sup>.
**2 [[Condemned Peng]]s spawn after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>, delay 46.67~50 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,500f</sup>.
**2 [[Ursamajor]]s spawn after 90 seconds<sup>2,700f</sup>, delay 60~63.33 seconds<sup>1,800f~1,900f</sup>.

==Strategy==
There are limited peons that spawn prior to the boss wave, so stalling to build up your wallet is actually quite easy, and will heavily benefit you.

After that, the stage is exceedingly simple. Cumulus Gallus is supported by Deonil, the occasional peon and, eventually, two Ursamajors. None of these threats have significant pushing power. A Lv.50 [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] can be spammed using Research [[Cat Combo]]s to very quickly get rid of the Behemoths, ideally without meatshielding so that Deonil has less chances to Freeze oncoming Couriers. [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]] and [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] will handle the supporting peons with relative ease.

From there, chip down Ursamajors gradually, or chain them using [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]].

